# Disable Energy Efficient Ethernet whenever the interface appears.
#
# This replaces a systemd unit bound to sys-subsystem-net-devices-eth0.device,
# which SILENTLY FAILED TO RUN on a fresh boot: the unit was enabled, the symlink
# was in place, the device unit was active (plugged), and the service never
# started. Two nodes had EEE off and one had it on, and nothing reported a
# problem. A mitigation that stops applying without saying so is worse than none,
# because it makes every subsequent measurement untrustworthy.
#
# udev fires on the device event itself, which is the thing that actually
# happens, and it re-fires whenever the interface is re-added -- including after
# the sentinel bounces the link.
#
# Note that EEE has been EXONERATED as the cause of the blackholes: worker-1
# blackholed with EEE off for 9.5 hours beforehand. This stays only so the
# variable remains controlled while the real cause is still open.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="net", KERNEL=="eth0", RUN+="/usr/sbin/ethtool --set-eee eth0 eee off"
